From ae600ae4c4f2001eb0a9f36f7ce796e2aa1533e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abyss <abyss@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:38:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] abyss: CED-aware prefill for DeepSeek V4.1
 (ABYSS_CED_PREFILL=1, ABYSS_CED_ALIGN=1)

A decoder layer needs a token's queries and FFN only where an output token, or the next decode step, still reaches
it through the sliding windows of the layers above. llama_context::ced_plan() works that out for each llama_decode()
call, and the V4.1 graph computes the queries, the index scores, the top-k masks and the FFN of each decoder layer
only for those tokens; every token still writes its KV.

The plan covers one sequence and never decreases along the batch, so the tokens a layer keeps are the last ones of
each ubatch: the graph takes them as views, and the scheduler uploads only those rows of the masks. A layer that
keeps no token computes no queries and no FFN. ABYSS_CED_ALIGN=1 puts the remainder of a call in its first ubatch,
so the last ubatch, which holds the tail the decoder layers run on, is full. ABYSS_CED_DEBUG=1 prints what each
ubatch keeps.
